    "title": "How to tell Boozer twins Cameron and Cayden apart as Carlos' Duke sons take on March Madness | Sporting News",
    "text": "The Duke Blue Devils have not one but two sons of Carlos Boozer on their men's basketball team.The two standout freshmen, twins Cameron and Cayden, are both now taking on March Madness as the top overall seed Duke tries to win a national championship. Despite being twins, though, the pair has plenty of differences, and in the national spotlight, they'll get plenty of attention.This is a bit more to know about each Boozer twin and how to tell them apart.MORE: The math behind a perfect bracket is unfathomableWhich Boozer twin is which?Jersey numbersCameron Boozer wears the number 12 for Duke.Cayden Boozer wears the number 2.HeightCameron Boozer is listed at 6-foot-9, 250 pounds and is a forward.Cayden Boozer is listed at 6-foot-4 and 205 pounds, a guard.TalentCameron Boozer is one of the three best freshmen in college basketball, along with BYU's AJ Dybantsa and Kansas' Darryn Peterson. They're favored to be the top-three picks in the 2026 NBA Draft, and Boozer is considered by most to be the national player of the year.Cayden is a good player and will likely make it to the NBA, but he won't necessarily end up as a lottery pick, and he might stay at Duke longer than a year.But put them together, and they've got a chance to lead Duke to great heights.More March Madness news:Michigan has a fascinating path in the Midwest RegionWe now know how Duke can get to the Final FourUsing a 28-year streak to pick a bracket national championCaleb Wilson shares honest feelings about staying at UNC",
